0..80 Comment "//! Copy-on-write: a copy of a long string shares its buffer and counts one more"
81..159 Comment "//! holder, and a write copies the buffer only when another string holds it; a"
160..240 Comment "//! buffer held once is written in place. A short string\'s bytes are its own, so"
241..321 Comment "//! its copy is a copy of at most the inline capacity. Either way a write to one"
322..362 Comment "//! string is never seen through another"
363..439 Comment "//! [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics], § 3."
440..443 Comment "//!"
444..471 Comment "//! - see: #1481 — `long`"
472..550 Comment "//! - cites: [Racordon-2022-implementation_strategies_mutable_value_semantics]"
551..554 Comment "//!"
